{#
  One person, for the Person column of JUser's user index.

  **This is the host's half of a contract JUser declares**, named through
  `juser_person_template` on `JUser\Twig\JUserExtension`. JUser has no person model — only
  `PersonValueOptionsProviderInterface` and whatever rows this application answers it with —
  so the module includes this with the row as `person` and knows nothing else about it.

  A one-line template rather than the macro call inlined into JUser's own index, which is
  what it was before 2026-08-21: the module cannot import a template it does not ship, and a
  Twig function returning pre-escaped HTML would be the same coupling with worse failure
  modes.

  `fmt.person()` reproduces the laminas `FormatPerson` view helper, pencil included. JUser
  passed `['editPencil' => true]` to the helper, which reads `displayEditPencil` and so has
  never read that key — the default, pencil on, is what both sides have always rendered.

  Whitespace is trimmed at both ends because this lands inside a `<td>`.
#}
{%- import 'schoenstatt/_entity-format.html.twig' as fmt -%}
{{- fmt.person(person) -}}
